{
  "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
  "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192e101bf39-0000-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nALLYSON N. HO, ESQUIRE, Dallas, Texas; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nANTHONY A. YANG, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioner.\nC. KEVIN MARSHALL, ESQUIRE, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Debtor Respondents.\nDAVID C. FREDERICK, ESQUIRE, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Claimant Respondents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192e101bf39-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(11:37 a.m.) CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument next in Case 22-1079, Truck Insurance Exchange versus Kaiser Gypsum Company. Ms. Ho."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Allyson N. Ho",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192e101bf39-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If anyone is a party in interest entitled to be heard in this Chapter 11 case, it's the insurer, Truck, who will pay virtually every dollar the debtors owe the asbestos claimants."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192e101bf39-0001-0001",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Both counterparties to executory contracts and creditors are parties in interest that may be -- appear and be heard on any issue in a Chapter 11 bankruptcy case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192e101bf39-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I love asking this question. How do I write this so that there is a difference between that employee and the truck company?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192e101bf39-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF C. KEVIN MARSHALL FOR THE DEBTOR RESPONDENTS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "C. Kevin Marshall",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192e101bf39-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The list of parties in interest in Section 1109(b) shows this."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192e101bf39-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Isn't it just common sense that an insurer at the outset is going to have an interest in this because how much the insurer will have to pay will be affected by how the plan is structured?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192e101bf39-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Can I stop you a moment? I am looking at the brief of amici American Prosperity Casualty Insurance, and on page 15, they explain that once the plan is approved, this plan, under your terms, it obtains a discharge, the Debtor, and the protection of a channeling injunction, now all the claims are going to go through the trust and not to you."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "American Prosperity Casualty Insurance",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192e101bf39-0002-0003",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I am looking at the brief of amici American Prosperity Casualty Insurance, and on page 15, they explain that once the plan is approved, this plan, under your terms, it obtains a discharge, the Debtor, and the protection of a channeling injunction, now all the claims are going to go through the trust and not to you."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192e101bf39-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Would you object to permissive intervention in a situation like this where the insurer is seeking fraud prevention?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192e101bf39-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "BUT WHY -- WHY SHOULD YOU AS THE DEBTOR TRUST HAVE THAT ADVANTAGE AND NOT GIVE IT TO THEM?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192e101bf39-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "WHAT DOES THAT HAVE TO DO WITH THE --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192e101bf39-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 71,
        "start": 71
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "DO YOU HAVE ANYTHING IN THE TEXT THAT CAN SUGGEST THAT THE TEXT HAS INCORPORATED THAT VIEW?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192e101bf39-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "BUT I THINK YOU'VE ADMITTED THAT A COURT CAN DO THOSE PROVISIONS AND THEY HAVE DONE THEM IN OTHER CASES LAWFULLY, RIGHT?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192e101bf39-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 74,
        "start": 74
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "DO YOU AGREE ON ARTICLE III THAT -- THAT THAT'S WITH RESPECT TO A PLAINTIFF COMING TO COURT AND NOT WITH RESPECT TO THOSE WHO OBJECT UNDER BOND AND CLAPPER?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192e101bf39-0003-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "WELL, IF HE'S NOT IMPAIRED, DOESN'T HE HAVE AN INTEREST IN MAKING SURE THAT DOESN'T CHANGE?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2023-22-1079",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3192e101bf3975817c1ae1ea7ed56114831ef1d7f47d9a222b0bec52ba063b7e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3192e101bf39-0003-0009",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 85,
        "start": 85
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 12:50 p.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
